<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pericles</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 495–429 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pericles was an Athenian statesman and general who dominated the democracy from the 450s until his death in 429 BCE. He used the tribute of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delian-league">Delian League</a>, whose treasury had been moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, to fund the building programme of the Acropolis, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthenon">Parthenon</a>. He led Athens into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and died of the plague that struck the besieged city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pericles.jpg" alt="Pericles" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Copy of Kresilas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pericles_Pio-Clementino_Inv269_n2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
